Let the persistent console ring be pinned to a chosen device block
(liuqinlogblk=N).  The previous-boot tail dump and the flush thread share the base:
the default "last 4 MiB of the partition" is unreadable on this port, and the
dump's hung read kept the flush thread from ever writing a header, which is why
TWRP always found the area zero.  The base and any write error are drawn through
the mute gate.
